WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:24.240
 

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:24.740
When I'm asleep

00:00:24.820 --> 00:00:25.320
my brain

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:25.820
is

00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:28.040
still in motion.

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:29.880
I sort of see it

00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:33.000
like little pieces of fiber that are connecting.

00:00:34.660 --> 00:00:36.740
It's incredible how active my mind is

00:00:36.740 --> 00:00:39.760
when I'm supposed to be laying asleep .

00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:41.240
When I'm asleep

00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:42.840
my brain is active and,

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:44.940
and going around.

00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:50.980
When I'm awake in the day, my brain is like this; when I go to sleep at night

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:53.420
my brain is like this.

00:00:53.422 --> 00:00:54.479
Just waking up

00:00:55.390 --> 00:00:57.390
awake and

00:00:57.760 --> 00:01:01.380
sleeping, it's-- kind of tapers off to this just waking up point again.

00:01:03.820 --> 00:01:08.970
When you're asleep you're pretty much awake, but you don't know it.

00:01:13.150 --> 00:01:13.990
When I'm asleep,

00:01:13.990 --> 00:01:16.280
I think my cells are resting.

00:01:16.280 --> 00:01:16.780
 

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:19.120
Your brain needs time to recover and rest and

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:21.560
let synapses heal.

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:24.240
I think the stress is just too great for us nowadays.

00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:25.360
If we don't get

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:27.960
a minimum of seven hours sleep,

00:01:28.260 --> 00:01:29.800
we're in serious trouble.

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:31.900
My body needs

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:32.740
R E S T !

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:36.800
It needs to take off its job.

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:38.440
It does a lot.

00:01:38.440 --> 00:01:39.100
 

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:48.180
Sometimes I'm willing to face things when I'm asleep that I might not really want to

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:49.700
deal with when I'm awake.

00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:51.140
Maybe sort of a

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:54.680
kinda sexual dream, if you will, with maybe someone it shouldn't be with

00:01:54.680 --> 00:01:55.360
 

00:01:55.360 --> 00:02:01.820
Maybe I'm attracted to somebody and in my dreams I'm really flirtatious, then if I come across this person again

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:03.960
I think I'll flirt a little bit more.

00:02:04.280 --> 00:02:06.020
My dreams

00:02:06.040 --> 00:02:11.540
sometimes are just like maybe scenes from stuff

00:02:11.660 --> 00:02:14.800
I watch--you know--like Star Wars or Batman the Animated Series.

00:02:15.440 --> 00:02:21.920
And so I'm seeing like scenes from-- that it's like scene after scene 
after scene that it's like....

00:02:23.460 --> 00:02:27.220
I was sort of driving around in a small clown car of some reason

00:02:28.060 --> 00:02:33.330
talking to Albert Einstein, Newton and I remember specifically them telling me that

00:02:33.489 --> 00:02:35.338
two plus two did not equal four.

00:02:35.338 --> 00:02:38.699
I'm flying through like an endless hole, and I actually feel

00:02:39.640 --> 00:02:41.640
like if I'm actually falling

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:46.738
Well, that's a good question.

00:02:46.738 --> 00:02:47.238
Where does my mind go?

00:02:47.720 --> 00:02:50.300
I don't really know.

00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:50.800
Mine is searching for solutions.

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:52.560
It can't be ON all the time.

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:53.060
My mind's awake, but

00:02:53.330 --> 00:02:54.290
I'm sleeping.

00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:55.980
 

00:02:55.980 --> 00:02:57.980
 

00:02:58.080 --> 00:03:00.860
I don't know about dreams. I think it's important.

00:03:00.860 --> 00:03:06.500
Maybe it's not that important.  Sleep and dreams are such an insight into yourself and your own challenges.

