Parts of the brain can sleep more deeply than other parts at the same time and a lot of our current

00:17:27.699 --> 00:17:30.239
thoughts about the function of sleep and

00:17:31.840 --> 00:17:37.260
Based on this local aspect of sleep were derived from these studies with the marine mammals and

00:17:38.170 --> 00:17:39.280
this

00:17:39.280 --> 00:17:47.160
Modulation of sleep intensity locally in the brain seems to be related to how we use certain parts of the brain during wakefulness

00:17:47.530 --> 00:17:55.139
So so a region we might be using a lot might go into a deep sleep yet when we're asleep. Yeah, so

00:17:55.900 --> 00:17:57.520
if

00:17:57.520 --> 00:18:04.589
Somebody did a certain task with their hand that part of the brain connected to that will sleep more deeply

00:18:05.260 --> 00:18:11.010
Afterwards and you can even do the opposite and their studies showing that if you immobilize an arm

00:18:11.890 --> 00:18:19.890
For a day then the part of the brain that controls that arm shows lighter sleep that night, so we're clearly

00:18:20.560 --> 00:18:26.249
Getting something out of sleep and in a way some of the demands in our waking life

00:18:26.730 --> 00:18:32.910
Make make us need to get more of it for those particular area, so there's something about sleep is it

00:18:33.550 --> 00:18:38.550
You know restoring our energy? I mean. Why would a choral or a fly need to sleep?

00:18:38.550 --> 00:18:42.839
You know like we do - and what did what's the currency there that we all?

